CSS FOR THE HEADER.
Every clean stylesheet starts with two foundational pieces:

The Universal Reset (*): Browsers add invisible default margin and padding around elements (like <body> and <ul>), 
and calculate widths awkwardly by default. Resetting margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; gives you a
predictable blank canvas where padding doesn't unexpectedly inflate element widths.

CSS Custom Properties (Variables) in :root: Instead of typing hex codes (#F04D07, #000000, #989999, #891A06)
repeatedly across dozens of rules, define them once inside :root (for example, --color-bg: #000000; and --color-accent: #F04D07;) 
and reuse them anywhere via var(--color-accent).

